-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">All-on-4 dental implants</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Implants &amp; oral surgery</p><h1>All-on-4 dental implants</h1><p class="detail-lead">Ask the team about full-arch implant options and the evaluation involved in determining whether they fit your circumstances.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">A full-arch conversation, not a one-size-fits-all promise.</h2><p class="intro-large">A fixed full-arch restoration supported by implants may be an option for people missing many or all teeth in one arch. “All-on-4” describes one approach, not a universal treatment plan.</p><p>Evaluation includes jaw anatomy, remaining teeth, bite, medical factors, maintenance needs and alternative treatments. The number and location of implants depend on clinical planning.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Review the goals</h3><p>Discuss chewing, appearance, function, cleaning requirements and what has been difficult with existing teeth or dentures.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Evaluate candidacy</h3><p>The dental team considers imaging, bone and soft tissues, medical history and whether specialist care is indicated.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Plan the sequence</h3><p>Treatment can involve surgical, temporary and final restorative phases with follow-up over time.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Does everyone receive teeth on the same day?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Immediate temporary restorations depend on clinical conditions and should not be assumed.</p></details><details><summary>Is a full-arch implant bridge removable?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Some full-arch restorations are fixed and others removable; ask which design is proposed and how it is maintained.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Dentures</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/dentures/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
