-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Crowns &amp; bridges</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Restorative dentistry</p><h1>Crowns &amp; bridges</h1><p class="detail-lead">Ask about options for restoring a damaged tooth or replacing a missing one. The team can explain how crowns and bridges differ and when each is considered.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">Strength and function, thoughtfully restored.</h2><p class="intro-large">A crown covers a prepared tooth when a filling alone is not suitable. A bridge can replace a missing tooth by using supporting teeth or other appropriate structures.</p><p>Crowns and bridges have different implications for healthy neighboring teeth, cleaning and longevity. The right choice depends on what the dentist sees and the options available.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Evaluate the tooth or gap</h3><p>Examination and imaging help determine the amount of remaining tooth support and the treatment alternatives.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Plan the restoration</h3><p>Discuss materials, appearance, bite, number of visits and temporary restorations when necessary.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Fit and maintain</h3><p>Your dentist checks contacts and comfort; ongoing cleaning and reviews protect the restoration.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Is a crown always needed after a root canal?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Many back teeth benefit from added protection, but the recommendation depends on remaining tooth structure and bite forces.</p></details><details><summary>How does a bridge compare with an implant?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A bridge uses adjacent support; an implant replaces the missing tooth root. Health, anatomy, timing and preference influence the choice.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Dental implants</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/implants/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
