-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Dentures</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Restorative dentistry</p><h1>Dentures</h1><p class="detail-lead">Explore partial and full dentures and ask about fixed options where appropriate. The team can walk you through fit, care and follow-up.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">A more comfortable way forward.</h2><p class="intro-large">Full or partial dentures can replace missing teeth and support everyday function. Modern treatment planning considers appearance, fit, speech, chewing and long-term care.</p><p>Dentures need time for adjustment and may require future relining or replacement as the mouth changes. Implant-supported alternatives may be worth discussing when appropriate.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Talk about everyday needs</h3><p>Bring concerns about eating, speaking, denture stability and appearance.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Review your options</h3><p>Your dentist explains removable designs, fit considerations and when implant-supported options might be assessed.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Adjust over time</h3><p>A fitting and follow-up process helps address pressure points and changes in comfort.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Will dentures feel natural immediately?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>An adjustment period is common. Report persistent sore spots rather than trying to alter the denture yourself.</p></details><details><summary>Can I sleep wearing dentures?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Follow the dentist’s instructions. Many removable dentures are taken out overnight for cleaning and to rest the tissues.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Dental implants</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/implants/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
