-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Dental fillings</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Restorative dentistry</p><h1>Dental fillings</h1><p class="detail-lead">Discuss how a tooth can be restored and the materials available. Dr. Raina can also review existing fillings and explain what she recommends.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">Restore a tooth with purpose.</h2><p class="intro-large">When a tooth has decay or a damaged area, a filling can restore the affected portion while retaining healthy tooth structure where possible. Material choice is part of the treatment conversation.</p><p>The dentist assesses the extent of damage before recommending a filling. A larger or weakened tooth may require a different restoration, such as a crown.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Identify the problem</h3><p>An examination and indicated imaging help determine whether a restoration is needed.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Consider the material</h3><p>Discuss durability, appearance, tooth location, allergies or sensitivities and clinical suitability.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Restore and review</h3><p>After treatment, the bite and restoration are checked; your team explains home care and follow-up.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Can an old silver filling be replaced?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A dentist can evaluate its condition and the reasons for replacement. Intact amalgam should not routinely be removed solely for the purpose of removing mercury exposure.</p></details><details><summary>How do I know which filling material is right?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>There is no single material for every tooth. Discuss the size of the restoration, clinical requirements and personal preferences.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>SMART amalgam removal</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/smart/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
