-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Dental ozone therapy</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Signature care · Biological dentistry</p><h1>Dental ozone therapy</h1><p class="detail-lead">Raina lists dental ozone as an adjunct to some procedures. Discuss when the practice considers it, the limits of its use and the other options available.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Our considered approach</p><h2 id="overview">An adjunct, never a substitute for sound dental care.</h2><p class="intro-large">Dental ozone is a form of oxygen-based therapy that some practices use as an adjunct within selected dental procedures. Its proposed use, supporting evidence and limitations should be made clear before treatment.</p><p>Ozone therapy should not be presented as a replacement for examination, proven infection management, appropriate restoration or standard periodontal treatment. A clinician must determine whether it has a role in a specific care plan.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Identify the clinical need</h3><p>Start with a dental diagnosis and understand the established treatment options.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Clarify the proposed role</h3><p>Ask exactly where ozone would fit, what is expected and which outcomes are supported by evidence.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Understand the alternative</h3><p>Discuss whether conventional care alone is appropriate and how progress would be evaluated.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Can ozone replace a filling or root canal?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>It should not be assumed to replace established restorative or endodontic treatment.</p></details><details><summary>Is ozone suitable for everyone?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Suitability, precautions and whether it is offered must be reviewed by the treating clinician.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Appointments</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/appointments/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
