-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Periodontal treatment</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Restorative dentistry</p><h1>Periodontal treatment</h1><p class="detail-lead">Ask how the practice evaluates gum health and what it may recommend based on the findings.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">Healthy gums are the foundation.</h2><p class="intro-large">Gum inflammation and periodontal disease can affect the tissues and bone that support your teeth. Care begins with understanding the condition of the gums—not simply scheduling an ordinary cleaning.</p><p>Your clinician may measure gum pockets, assess bleeding and review imaging and risk factors. Treatment and maintenance vary depending on the findings.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Understand gum health</h3><p>An exam may look for inflammation, pocket depth, recession, mobility and signs of bone loss.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Make a targeted plan</h3><p>Professional treatment, daily hygiene adjustments and risk-factor counseling are considered as appropriate.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Protect the progress</h3><p>Periodontal maintenance is often more frequent than standard preventive visits; your team will explain the interval.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Why do my gums bleed when brushing?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Bleeding can be a sign of irritation or inflammation and merits assessment if recurring.</p></details><details><summary>Is gum disease reversible?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Early gingivitis can often improve with care; established periodontitis requires ongoing management and cannot always reverse lost support.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Exams &amp; cleanings</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/exams/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
