-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Enamel remineralization</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Prevention &amp; family</p><h1>Enamel remineralization</h1><p class="detail-lead">Explore ways to manage early enamel mineral changes and protect your teeth.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">Protecting enamel before damage advances.</h2><p class="intro-large">Early mineral changes in enamel may sometimes be stabilized with preventive care. Cavitated lesions and structural damage usually require different treatment.</p><p>The right strategy depends on individual decay risk, the stage of the lesion, oral hygiene and the patient’s preferences about preventive materials.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Assess the enamel</h3><p>The dentist looks for signs of early mineral loss and determines whether a lesion is reversible or requires restoration.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Choose prevention tools</h3><p>Review brushing, diet, saliva factors and preventive materials supported for the situation.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Monitor change</h3><p>Follow-up examination and imaging when indicated help evaluate whether the approach is working.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Can remineralization rebuild a missing piece of tooth?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. It can affect early mineral loss, not replace large defects or lost tooth anatomy.</p></details><details><summary>What if I prefer fluoride-free products?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Tell your dentist; discuss the evidence, tradeoffs and other available preventive measures.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Exams &amp; cleanings</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/exams/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
