-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Root canals</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Restorative dentistry</p><h1>Root canals</h1><p class="detail-lead">If a root canal has been recommended, ask what the visit involves and how the tooth would be restored afterward.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Your care, explained</p><h2 id="overview">Relief and tooth preservation.</h2><p class="intro-large">Root canal treatment addresses inflammation or infection inside a tooth. When the tooth can be saved, removing the affected tissue and sealing the canals may help preserve function.</p><p>Your dentist will explain the diagnosis, alternatives and what restoration is needed afterward. Some cases may require referral to an endodontist.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Confirm the diagnosis</h3><p>The clinician reviews symptoms, examination findings and indicated images.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Discuss treatment and comfort</h3><p>The procedure, anesthesia, possible referral and alternatives are explained before proceeding.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Restore and follow up</h3><p>A permanent filling or crown may be recommended to protect the treated tooth.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Is a root canal the same as an extraction?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Root canal treatment is intended to keep the tooth, while extraction removes it.</p></details><details><summary>Will a root-canal-treated tooth need a crown?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>It depends on tooth location, remaining structure and bite forces; discuss the final restoration as part of planning.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Crowns &amp; bridges</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/crowns/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
