-  <main class="detail-main treatment-page" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/care/">Treatments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">SMART amalgam removal</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Signature care · Materials</p><h1>SMART amalgam removal</h1><p class="detail-lead">SMART stands for Safe Mercury Amalgam Removal Technique, an IAOMT protocol. If a filling needs replacement, ask Dr. Raina about the precautions the practice uses and the materials available.</p><div class="detail-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call the practice <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></div><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><div class="editorial-body"><section class="editorial-intro" aria-labelledby="overview"><p class="eyebrow">Our considered approach</p><h2 id="overview">A safer conversation about silver fillings.</h2><p class="intro-large">SMART is the Safe Mercury Amalgam Removal Technique developed by the International Academy of Oral Medicine and Toxicology. It describes precautions intended to reduce exposure during removal of existing amalgam restorations.</p><p>An important distinction: deciding whether a filling needs replacement is different from deciding how a necessary removal should be performed. The FDA advises against removing intact amalgam fillings without a medical reason in most cases because doing so can remove healthy tooth structure and temporarily increase exposure.</p></section><section class="journey-section" aria-labelledby="journey"><p class="eyebrow">The experience</p><h2 id="journey">How we approach this care.</h2><ol class="journey-list"><li><span class="stage-index">01</span><div><h3>Assess the existing filling</h3><p>The dentist evaluates damage, recurrent decay, function and other clinical reasons for considering replacement.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">02</span><div><h3>Discuss materials and precautions</h3><p>If removal is appropriate, review the SMART protocol, isolation, air management and planned replacement material with the team.</p></div></li><li><span class="stage-index">03</span><div><h3>Plan restoration and follow-up</h3><p>Understand what will be placed in the tooth and what to expect after the visit.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="editorial-faq" aria-labelledby="questions"><p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p><h2 id="questions">Questions worth answering.</h2><div class="faq-stack"><details><summary>Should every silver filling be removed?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. The FDA generally recommends leaving intact amalgam restorations in place unless removal is medically necessary.</p></details><details><summary>Does SMART mean mercury is removed from the body?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. SMART is a procedural precaution protocol for dental amalgam removal; it is not a systemic detoxification treatment.</p></details></div></section><nav class="editorial-related" aria-label="Related care"><div><p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h3>Dental fillings</h3></div><a class="text-link" href="/care/fillings/">View related care <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></nav></div><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="editorial-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Here when you’re ready</p><h2>Care begins with a conversation.</h2><p>Tell us what matters to you. Our team can help you plan your next visit.</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Book an appointment <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">(630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div><div class="editorial-aside-note"><span class="aside-monogram" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p>Raina Dental Care<br>Naperville, Illinois</p></div></aside></div></main>
